    "verdict": "The cold-end silence (E_N min -> 0.00) IS reached under BOTH periodic and always-on drive (periodic min_E_N=0.000, always_on min_E_N=0.000 at b_k=-7.0). The reason is the settled convention b_S=b_k: the terminals cool with the interior, so the +D drive (competing with terminal bias b_k) holds S,T active at the operating point (term active rate always_on 0.98 at b_k=-2.0) but is OVERWHELMED at deep cooling (term active rate always_on 0.05 at b_k=-7.0). So under b_S=b_k the drive does NOT keep silence out of the accessible ensemble at the cold end, even always-on. The printed table's 0.00 is therefore consistent with this construction and does NOT by itself require a drive-off sweep -- but section IV-D's 'the drive removes silence' holds only near the operating point under this convention, and Proposition 2(i) now carries the claim analytically, so the table is corroboration, not load-bearing."
